method.description:
Returns a copy of the state of [param entity] at [param tick]. The record is empty when nothing was recorded.
[codeblock]
var past := api.lagcomp_sample(entity, tick)
if past.has_value(&"position"):
    print(past.position)
[/codeblock]

Disconnects and returns to [constant NetwSession.SESSION_STATE_OFFLINE]. On the server, it saves every persistent entity first, and a failed save keeps the session online. The promise resolves with an [enum @GlobalScope.Error] within three seconds.
[codeblock]
var left := api.session_leave()
if not left.is_settled:
    await left.wait()
if left.result != OK:
    push_error("still online: %s" % error_string(left.result))
[/codeblock]

Sets the join request sent when [member MultiplayerAPI.multiplayer_peer] connects. A server sends it at [method session_submit_join]. The promise result is an [enum @GlobalScope.Error].
[codeblock]
var prepared := api.session_prepare_join(&"Dev")
if not prepared.is_settled:
    await prepared.wait()
if int(prepared.result) != OK:
    return
[/codeblock]
An empty [param username] returns [constant @GlobalScope.ERR_INVALID_PARAMETER].
[b]Player request.[/b]

Registers the [NetwTransport] script [param type] with this session. Registering it again returns the same [RID]. Returns an invalid [RID] when another script is already registered for the same peer class. It replaces the built-in transport of that class.
[codeblock]
func _ready() -> void:
    var api := Netw.of(self)
    var relay := api.transport_register(MyRelayTransport)
    var caps: int = api.transport_get_param(
            relay, NetwMultiplayer.TRANSPORT_PARAM_CAPABILITIES)
[/codeblock]
